# Smol Biscuits SlimeVR Trackers
These are a derivative of SlimeVR trackers, designed to be smaller, lighter and longer lasting!

They consists of:
- Custom PCB
- Custom 3D printed case
- Custom firmware derived from SlimeVR firmware

## PCB
The PCB is designed in KiCad and the files can be found in the `pcb` folder. The PCB is designed to be as small as possible, acting as a carrier board for a Seeed Studio XIAO nrf52840 on the opposite side of the sensors.

The sensor board has an IMU and a magnetometer.

### IMU
> ICM-45686

### Magnetometer
> QMC-6309

## Battery
The board requires a LiPo batter. Size based on your needs, but the included case is designed to fit a 150mAh battery.

## 3D Printed Case
The case is a two-piece design with a flexible interlink. The battery is in one case and the PCB in the other.

The flexi-link allows the two piece design to bend around the body and also forms part of the strain relief for the battery cable.

The case files can be found in the `case` folder.

### Materials
- The flexi-link is designed to be printed in TPU.
- The base plates should be printed in PETG for strength. The strap piece is put under strain and may break if printed in PLA.
- The top cover can be printed in PLA or PETG, whatever you prefer.
- The switch can also be printed in whatever you prefer for aesthetics.